I can't deny, I'm one for hype and this for me did not feel hyped at all. For people into the Xcom crowd this is probably the best thing in the world. But now I've put in 32 POINT 7 hrs I can happily say it is the best thing in the world. This game seems so underrated and I'll be honest it was not on my radar at all until this years summer sale when it dropped down to 11 squids or so for the base game. I'll tell you now I'm scared of the DLC but the base game is amazing. I don't need to list the constant positive of this game because there are so many (If you want more detail I'll link a youtuber who I think judged the game fairly with his release copy, care language:
) and the game just works so well and does every little thing you want from a turn  based game. My favourite being the fact you can edit your characters in multiple different paths, e.g. when you want to edit your gun you are able to reach the weapon customisation from the deployment window or the armory and don't have to go one way like so many other games. It may seem futile but developers that give such small options are developers that make good games. This game is TOTALLY worth it's original release price 100%. No it is not for everyone because y'know it's turn based and I'll be honest if you don't like chess or being beaten up by a computer game you won't like this. It is HARD on higher difficulties and takes a lot of patience, especially on escorts where you are timed on your objective. There are options to go without saves and do it in one go if you wish, which I haven't done yet but I'll tell yopu now I have no problem with doing so. I love this kind of game and it is the best of its genre, I'm hooked man!
This is the kind of game you can play all day and feel satisfied as chuff after you're done. At the end of the day, you like turn base or you don't. But I tell you now this game is worth it's low release price and it's completely worth the 11 pound sale I tell you now.

